      "risk_review": {
        "status": "open",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-58-3a",
        "notes": "All eight current proof steps and every direct dependency were read. Exact domain/variance/composition uses match producer steps 1.1-2.2; scalar and even Dirac locality match open spacelike regions and extend by norm continuity, including empty regions. Positive SI scaling and momentum sign reversal preserve domains. DCT uses integrable rho or sigma times bounded tests; the Fourier transform tends to one, finite shell annuli are dominated by one, and radial density r^2/(4 pi^2 sqrt(r^2+mu^2)) gives unbounded annular mass for every mu>=0. Spatial L2 scaling and equal-time CAR yield operator norm >= L2 norm/sqrt(2). Countable Choice is inherited, no empirical inputs enter, and no other point constructions are excluded. Consumer local argument is sound, but reader:58:1 and refuter:58:1 retain an unresolved batch-43 public-claim defect: generic smooth point-mass approximants are not the fixed bump families proved there. Producer current raw hash remains ca830cee0b04026607347571b9f93ebef157317cfa2ecc5f27ad0c04a19131de. Owner must resolve producer quantifier/profile scope and consumers before closure. Exact pre-reader consumer bytes were also not recovered; no authorized current-content historical disposition was found. Risk review intentionally remains open.",
