      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-58-3a",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps against exact current direct suppliers. Compact smooth variations make action differences finite without globally integrable fields; the scalar sign is Box-mu^2=-(partial_0^2-Delta+mu^2). Both scalar shell vectors vanish, including the conjugated test. Dirac Schwartz decay removes integration-by-parts boundary terms and gives u_LF=0. beta L=i gamma^a partial_a-mu is an identity of differential expressions; no inference Psi(beta LF)=beta Psi(LF) is used. Stationarity iff equations follows in both directions from the commuting-field variation lemma. mu=0 and zero tests are admitted, Countable Choice is inherited without stronger selection. Representations and statistics remain adopted postulates, with no empirical premises or quantization deduction. Draft and existing outside workflow holds are retained; no full transitive audit is claimed.",
        "prior_reviews": [
          {
