      "risk_review": {
        "status": "open",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-58-3a",
        "notes": "Checked both current steps. Positive-definite Q makes the displayed normalized Gaussian a nonnegative Schwartz density with integral one; the theorem covers its translated anisotropic cases. DCT has the explicit integrable majorant ||g||_infty rho and is applied along arbitrary positive width sequences. epsilon_n=(1 metre)/n produces divergent vacuum norms, so finite Fock norm convergence is impossible. mu=0 is included by the theorem; no general point-field, renormalization or empirical claim follows. The counterexample local proof is sound. Closure remains blocked by the theorem dependency producer findings and missing exact pre-reader counterexample bytes; no historical current-content owner resolution found.",
